From 5ddcd468f008ea54f0d6e4504063776e10b8b8a8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: proshiv85-byte <proshiv85@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 11:46:15 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] SystemUI: add a large condensed clock style for the AOD

On AOD, show a large condensed clock (Roboto Flex at its narrowest
width and display optical size), the date and a battery pill, centered
in the upper part of the screen, with the AOD notification icons
centered below them. A black scrim, raised with translationZ, hides the
stock clock and smartspace while dozing.

Leaving AOD, the clock rises, shrinks and loosens from condensed to
regular width with emphasized easing while the date and battery fade
first; the scrim then fades to reveal the lockscreen, whose own clock
animates in. Entering AOD plays the motion in reverse, with the content
fading in once the scrim has covered the lockscreen. Pulsing fades the
style out so the stock pulse UI shows, and burn-in offsets glide once a
minute.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
